{"notebook":"nb1","page":7,"seed":7,"says":"Wood is a tone before it is a line. Agreed, and you have also just told me how to draw noon. The window is lying on the floorboards now, four panes of light, so I am doing exactly what you said: a blunt tip over everything the sun misses, three passes, darker away from the glass, and the lit patch left as bare paper. I get my white and you get your graphite; this may be the one page where we want the same thing. The cat is mine, though. She goes in the best pane, drawn first while the point is still sharp.","before":{"length":151.8616124626031,"worn":0.025951237688292765,"eraser":10.898879256580623,"sharpenings":8,"graphite":6.699051341555869,"distance":133870.8905328485},"after":{"length":148.39205680120185,"worn":0.06485958905077122,"eraser":10.898879256580623,"sharpenings":9,"graphite":7.471551797567298,"distance":164627.22816589585},"stats":{"strokeM":30.756337633043024,"graphite":0.7725004560113786,"used":3.4695556614012446,"sharpenings":1,"erasedMm2":0,"coverage":0.03550746716910309,"stopped":false},"warnings":[],"ops":[{"op":"write","text":"12:10. The window on the floor.","x":14,"y":22,"size":7},{"op":"curve","points":[[90,108],[94,102],[102,100],[110,103],[113,110],[111,117],[104,121],[96,121],[90,117]],"closed":true,"pressure":0.9},{"op":"circle","cx":93.5,"cy":114.5,"r":4.6,"pressure":0.9},{"op":"polyline","points":[[90,112],[88.6,107.8],[92.4,110]],"pressure":0.9},{"op":"polyline","points":[[95,110.2],[97.6,106.6],[98,111.6]],"pressure":0.9},{"op":"curve","points":[[91.5,115],[92.5,115.8],[93.5,115]],"pressure":0.8},{"op":"curve","points":[[112,113],[112,121],[104,124.5],[95,123],[90.5,119.5]],"pressure":1.1,"repeat":2},{"op":"hatch","region":{"polygon":[[97,104],[102,101.5],[109,104],[112,110],[110,116],[104,119.5],[99.5,119],[99,111]]},"angle":-30,"spacing":1.1,"pressure":0.6},{"op":"hatch","region":{"polygon":[[104,112],[111,110],[110,116.5],[104,120]]},"angle":40,"spacing":0.8,"pressure":0.8},{"op":"curve",